<!--
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 The Atalaia contributors
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

The opt-in network policy of a build made with -Patalaia.cleartextLan=true
(security review APP-3): cleartext HTTP to any address, which is what
Android's manifest flag did for every build before. Android cannot name an
address range, so a field whose controller's console has no fixed address
(a phone hotspot, a router's DHCP) needs this. It only reaches the web view
and Java networking; the app's own clients are not under it (see
network_security_config.xml). Every other build uses that stricter file.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="system" />
        </trust-anchors>
    </base-config>
</network-security-config>
